# /etc/cron.d/parec — monthly Rohlik spend report
#
# Install (as root):
#   install -m 0644 -o root -g root \
#     /mnt/prog/parec/.cron/parec.cron /etc/cron.d/parec
#   # cron.d file names must not contain dots; the trailing ".cron"
#   # extension is dropped on install.
#
# What it does:
#   On the 1st of every month at 07:00 local time, runs the parec
#   wrapper script as user `llm`. Stdout becomes the email body via
#   MAILTO; stderr (progress bars, debug noise) is redirected to a
#   log file inside the repo by the wrapper.
#
# Prerequisites on the host (all created/installed by `make install-cron`):
#   - /usr/local/bin/parec            — built binary
#   - /usr/local/bin/parec-monthly    — wrapper invoked below
#   - /etc/parec/parec.env            — credentials (root:$CRON_USER 0640)
#   - /var/lib/parec/                 — state dir owned by $CRON_USER
#
# Also required (NOT installed by make):
#   - Headless Chrome / Chromium on $PATH so chromedp can drive the login
#     flow (the package default is Headless=true).
#   - `msmtp` installed AND ~/.msmtprc (or /etc/msmtprc) configured for
#     the cron user — Gmail SMTP with an app password works fine. See
#     .cron/msmtprc.example in the repo. The wrapper composes + sends
#     the report itself, so MAILTO and a local MTA are not needed.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
# MAILTO intentionally unset — delivery is handled by parec-monthly via msmtp.
MAILTO=""

# The "__CRON_USER__" placeholder below is substituted by `make
# install-cron` with the value of CRON_USER (defaults to $(USER) — the
# account that ran make). Hand-installing the file? Replace the
# placeholder yourself before copying to /etc/cron.d/parec.
#
# m h dom mon dow user            command
0 7 1 * * __CRON_USER__ /usr/local/bin/parec-monthly
